@lang en
IMPORT `pti-tests-fixtures`

-- TESTS for Part 2 (the benefits) and for the assessment (waiting periods, limits, other
-- insurance, several layers at once). Expected values are worked by hand from the Rules'
-- words and from the fixtures' hypothetical figures (pti-tests-fixtures.l4 lists them):
-- Programme I sum insured 100m, main 120m, medical 20m; Programme II main 200m, benefit 1
-- 50m, bed 1m a day, benefit 2 60m, benefit 3 40m, before admission 5m, after discharge 5m,
-- home nursing 3m, allowance 200k a day up to 6m; outpatient 1m a visit, 10m in all;
-- dental and maternity co-payment 20%, limits 5m and 30m, newborn 5m; income allowance 300k
-- a day up to 9m; benefit 6 sum insured 50m. A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Tests — Part 2 and the assessment`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN e IS A `The event`
      pol IS A `The policy`
      it IS A `A claim item`
GIVETH A `The outcome for an item`
`the outcome, for the event` e `under` pol `, of` it MEANS
    `the outcome of the line` it `in` (`a claim by` `the insured person` `under` pol `for` e `with the lines` (LIST it))

GIVEN e IS A `The event`
      pol IS A `The policy`
      counted IS A LIST OF `An amount counted against a limit`
      it IS A `A claim item`
GIVETH A `The outcome for an item`
`the outcome, for the event` e `under` pol `, counting` counted `, of` it MEANS
    `the outcome for` (`the line` it `in` (`a claim by` `the insured person` `under` pol `for` e `with the lines` (LIST it))) `, given what was counted before:` counted

GIVEN p IS A `The insured person`
      e IS A `The event`
      pol IS A `The policy`
      it IS A `A claim item`
GIVETH A `The outcome for an item`
`the outcome, for` p `, for the event` e `under` pol `, of` it MEANS
    `the outcome of the line` it `in` (`a claim by` p `under` pol `for` e `with the lines` (LIST it))

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      l IS A `A limit`
GIVETH A LIST OF `An amount counted against a limit`
`already` n `against` l MEANS
    LIST (`An amount counted against a limit` WITH `the limit` IS l, `the amount` IS n)

-- A line during the stay whose reasonable amount differs from the charge.
GIVEN b IS A `A benefit`
      h IS A `A head of cost`
      d IS A DATE
      amt IS A NUMBER
      r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A claim item`
`a line under` b `for` h `on` d `charged` amt `, reasonable` r MEANS
    `A claim item` WITH
        `the benefit`                                  IS b
        `the head of cost`                             IS h
        `the date`                                     IS d
        `the amount charged`                           IS amt
        `the reasonable and customary amount`          IS r
        `the treatments it involves`                   IS EMPTY
        `the order`                                    IS JUST `a licensed doctor`
        `given during the hospital stay`               IS TRUE
        `the place of treatment`                       IS `a hospital in Vietnam`
        `directly related to the illness or injury for which the insured person was then admitted` IS TRUE
        `the insured person was in a critical condition threatening life and needing emergency treatment` IS FALSE
        `the main benefit it belongs to`               IS NOTHING
        `the visit`                                    IS 0
        `a visit to one specialty of one medical establishment, with tests or diagnostics, a specific diagnosis and a doctor's order for treatment` IS TRUE
        `the prescription was paid once already`       IS FALSE

-- A line during the stay at a given place.
GIVEN b IS A `A benefit`
      h IS A `A head of cost`
      d IS A DATE
      amt IS A NUMBER
      pl IS A `The place of treatment`
GIVETH A `A claim item`
`a line during the stay under` b `for` h `on` d `of` amt `at` pl MEANS
    `A claim item` WITH
        `the benefit`                                  IS b
        `the head of cost`                             IS h
        `the date`                                     IS d
        `the amount charged`                           IS amt
        `the reasonable and customary amount`          IS amt
        `the treatments it involves`                   IS EMPTY
        `the order`                                    IS JUST `a licensed doctor`
        `given during the hospital stay`               IS TRUE
        `the place of treatment`                       IS pl
        `directly related to the illness or injury for which the insured person was then admitted` IS TRUE
        `the insured person was in a critical condition threatening life and needing emergency treatment` IS FALSE
        `the main benefit it belongs to`               IS NOTHING
        `the visit`                                    IS 0
        `a visit to one specialty of one medical establishment, with tests or diagnostics, a specific diagnosis and a doctor's order for treatment` IS TRUE
        `the prescription was paid once already`       IS FALSE

-- A transport line on 1 March 2026, 2m.
GIVEN h IS A `A head of cost`
      critical IS A BOOLEAN
      mb IS A MAYBE `A benefit`
      o IS A MAYBE `The doctor who gave the order`
GIVETH A `A claim item`
`a transport line by` h `, critical:` critical `, going with` mb `, ordered by` o MEANS
    `A claim item` WITH
        `the benefit`                                  IS `Programme II other benefit: transport`
        `the head of cost`                             IS h
        `the date`                                     IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `the amount charged`                           IS 2_000_000
        `the reasonable and customary amount`          IS 2_000_000
        `the treatments it involves`                   IS EMPTY
        `the order`                                    IS o
        `given during the hospital stay`               IS FALSE
        `the place of treatment`                       IS `a hospital in Vietnam`
        `directly related to the illness or injury for which the insured person was then admitted` IS TRUE
        `the insured person was in a critical condition threatening life and needing emergency treatment` IS critical
        `the main benefit it belongs to`               IS mb
        `the visit`                                    IS 0
        `a visit to one specialty of one medical establishment, with tests or diagnostics, a specific diagnosis and a doctor's order for treatment` IS TRUE
        `the prescription was paid once already`       IS FALSE

-- Events.
GIVEN cause IS A `A cause`
      acc IS A MAYBE `The accident`
      ill IS A MAYBE `The illness`
      death IS A MAYBE DATE
      dis IS A MAYBE `The disablement`
      st IS A MAYBE `The hospital stay`
      diag IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `The event`
`an event of` cause `with accident` acc `, illness` ill `, death` death `, disablement` dis `, stay` st `, outpatient diagnosis` diag MEANS
    `The event` WITH
        `the cause`                                IS cause
        `the accident`                             IS acc
        `the illness`                              IS ill
        `the conditions diagnosed`                 IS LIST `a condition the Rules do not name`
        `the circumstances`                        IS EMPTY
        `the sporting activity`                    IS NOTHING
        `the hospital stay`                        IS st
        `the date of death`                        IS death
        `the cause of death unknown`               IS FALSE
        `the disablement`                          IS dis
        `the date the surgery was first ordered`   IS NOTHING
        `the date of the outpatient diagnosis`     IS diag

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The event`
`the standard accident, with death on` d MEANS
    `an event of` `an accident` `with accident` (JUST `the standard accident`) `, illness` NOTHING `, death` (JUST d) `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING

GIVEN dis IS A `The disablement`
GIVETH A `The event`
`the standard accident, with the disablement` dis MEANS
    `an event of` `an accident` `with accident` (JUST `the standard accident`) `, illness` NOTHING `, death` NOTHING `, disablement` (JUST dis) `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The event`
`the standard illness, with death on` d MEANS
    `an event of` `an illness` `with accident` NOTHING `, illness` (JUST `the standard illness`) `, death` (JUST d) `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING

GIVEN dis IS A `The disablement`
GIVETH A `The event`
`the standard illness, with the disablement` dis MEANS
    `an event of` `an illness` `with accident` NOTHING `, illness` (JUST `the standard illness`) `, death` NOTHING `, disablement` (JUST dis) `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING

`an outpatient illness` MEANS
    `an event of` `an illness` `with accident` NOTHING `, illness` (JUST `the standard illness`) `, death` NOTHING `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1))

`an occupational disease` MEANS
    `an event of` `an occupational disease` `with accident` NOTHING `, illness` (JUST `the standard illness`) `, death` NOTHING `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))

`a birth` MEANS
    `an event of` `pregnancy or childbirth` `with accident` NOTHING `, illness` NOTHING `, death` NOTHING `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` (JUST `the standard stay`) `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING

GIVEN adm IS A DATE
      dis IS A DATE
GIVETH A `The event`
`an illness with a stay from` adm `to` dis MEANS
    `an illness, with the stay` (`a stay from` adm `to` dis `, hours` 50 `, admitted` TRUE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a hospital in Vietnam`)

`the continuous policy` MEANS `a policy renewed continuously since 2023 on` `the full schedule`

`the doctor's order` MEANS JUST `a licensed doctor`

§§ `Programme I — personal accident`
-- Death 9 days after the accident: 100% of the sum insured.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with death on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS `payable` 100_000_000
-- Death on the last day of the 104 weeks (728 days after the accident), and the day after.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with death on` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 728)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 728)) EQUALS `payable` 100_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with death on` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 729)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 729)) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Total permanent disablement listed in the table, beginning 4 days after: 100%.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with the disablement` (`a disablement from` (YMD 2026 3 5) `lasting` 1 `weeks, listed as total:` TRUE `, partial rate:` NOTHING)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: total permanent disablement from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 5)) EQUALS `payable` 100_000_000
-- One that begins 729 days after the accident: outside the 104 weeks.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with the disablement` (`a disablement from` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 729) `lasting` 1 `weeks, listed as total:` TRUE `, partial rate:` NOTHING)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: total permanent disablement from an accident` `on` ((YMD 2026 3 1) PLUS 729)) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Partial, at the table's 25%: 25% of 100m.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with the disablement` (`a disablement from` (YMD 2026 3 5) `lasting` 60 `weeks, listed as total:` FALSE `, partial rate:` (JUST 25))) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: partial permanent disablement from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 5)) EQUALS `payable` 25_000_000
-- Partial under definition 17's second limb, which the table does not list: no rate.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the amount paid on` (`the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with the disablement` (`a disablement from` (YMD 2026 3 5) `lasting` 52 `weeks, listed as total:` FALSE `, partial rate:` NOTHING)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: partial permanent disablement from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 5))) BECAUSE "the Rules give no rate for a partial permanent disablement that Appendix 03 does not list"
-- Medical expenses: charged 5m, of which 4m reasonable: 4m.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard accident event` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `charged` 5_000_000 `, reasonable` 4_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 4_000_000
-- 25m of medical expenses: the 20m limit.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard accident event` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 25_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 20_000_000
-- 5m when 18m has already been counted against the 20m: 2m.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard accident event` `under` `the standard policy` `, counting` (`already` 18_000_000 `against` (`the limit for` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury`)) `, of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 5_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 2_000_000
-- Total disablement when 30m has already been counted against Programme I's 120m: 90m.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with the disablement` (`a disablement from` (YMD 2026 3 5) `lasting` 1 `weeks, listed as total:` TRUE `, partial rate:` NOTHING)) `under` `the standard policy` `, counting` (`already` 30_000_000 `against` (`the main limit of` `Programme I`)) `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: total permanent disablement from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 5)) EQUALS `payable` 90_000_000
-- Occupational disease: medicine 1m, paid; the same line for an ordinary illness is not.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `an occupational disease` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an occupational disease` `for` `medicines` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 1_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `an outpatient illness` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an occupational disease` `for` `medicines` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- The surgeon is not a head of Programme I's medical expenses as the Rules list them.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard accident event` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a line under` `Programme I: medical expenses for an accidental injury` `for` `the surgeon` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 1_000_000) EQUALS `not covered` `the head of cost is not one the benefit pays`
-- Programme I not bought.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`the standard accident, with death on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) `under` (`a first-year policy on` `Programme II alone`) `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10)) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit was not bought`
-- An accident on 20 December 2025, before cover took effect.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an event of` `an accident` `with accident` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2025 12 20) `of the kind` `an accident in daily life`)) `, illness` NOTHING `, death` (JUST (YMD 2025 12 25)) `, disablement` NOTHING `, stay` NOTHING `, outpatient diagnosis` NOTHING) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme I: death from an accident` `on` (YMD 2025 12 25)) EQUALS `not covered` `the event is outside the period of insurance`

§§ `Programme II — benefits 1, 2 and 3`
-- Benefit 1, the bed: 4m charged over three days, within 1m a day: 3m.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `the bed` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 4_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 3_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `(IV) physiotherapy` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `the surgeon` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 2_000_000) EQUALS `not covered` `the head of cost is not one the benefit pays`
-- 60m of medicines: the 50m limit for benefit 1.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness` `for` `(I) medicines used during the hospital stay` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 60_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 50_000_000
-- A stay of 23 hours is not a hospitalisation (definition 31).
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness, with the stay` (`a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 2) `, hours` 23 `, admitted` TRUE `, overnight` TRUE `, at` `a hospital in Vietnam`)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` `a clean benefit 1 line` EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Programme II is for illness, not accident.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard accident event` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` `a clean benefit 1 line` EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Benefit 2: the surgeon 30m; 70m against the 60m limit; an exploratory procedure is not paid.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `the surgeon` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 30_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `the surgeon` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 70_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 60_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness` `for` `an exploratory or diagnostic procedure` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 3_000_000) EQUALS `not covered` `the head of cost is not one the benefit pays`
-- Benefit 3: the transplant surgery 35m; buying the organ is not paid.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 3: organ transplant` `for` `surgery` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 35_000_000) EQUALS `payable` 35_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a line under` `Programme II benefit 3: organ transplant` `for` `buying the organ` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 35_000_000) EQUALS `not covered` `the head of cost is not one the benefit pays`

§§ `Programme II — the other benefits`
-- Before admission (admitted 1 May 2026): 1 April is the 30th day before, paid; 31 March
-- is not; the day of admission is not; without a doctor's order it is not.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `to` (YMD 2026 5 3)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: costs before admission` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 500_000
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `to` (YMD 2026 5 3)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: costs before admission` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 3 31) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `to` (YMD 2026 5 3)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: costs before admission` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 5 1) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 5 1) `to` (YMD 2026 5 3)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: costs before admission` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 4 1) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- After discharge (discharged 3 March 2026): 17 April is the 45th day after, paid; 18 April
-- is not; the day of discharge is not.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: treatment after discharge` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 4 17) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 500_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: treatment after discharge` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 4 18) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: treatment after discharge` `for` `examination` `on` (YMD 2026 3 3) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Home nursing after a 7-day stay (1-7 March): 22 March is the 15th day after discharge,
-- paid; 23 March is not. After a 6-day stay (1-6 March): not.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 7)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: home nursing` `for` `hiring a nurse` `on` (YMD 2026 3 22) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `the insured person's home in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 1_000_000
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 7)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: home nursing` `for` `hiring a nurse` `on` (YMD 2026 3 23) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `the insured person's home in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 3 6)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `Programme II other benefit: home nursing` `for` `hiring a nurse` `on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `of` 1_000_000 `at` `the insured person's home in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- The daily allowance: three days at 200k; forty days at 200k is 8m, within the 6m limit.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme II other benefit: daily hospital allowance` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) EQUALS `payable` 600_000
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` (`an illness with a stay from` (YMD 2026 3 1) `to` (YMD 2026 4 9)) `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`a fixed-sum line under` `Programme II other benefit: daily hospital allowance` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1)) EQUALS `payable` 6_000_000
-- Transport: an ambulance in a critical condition, going with benefit 1: 2m.
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `an ambulance of a hospital, of a lawful clinic, or of the 115 service` `, critical:` TRUE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`) `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `payable` 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `an ambulance of a hospital, of a lawful clinic, or of the 115 service` `, critical:` FALSE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`) `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `a taxi` `, critical:` TRUE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 2: surgery for illness`) `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `payable` 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `transport from a lower-level to a higher-level hospital in Vietnam` `, critical:` FALSE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`) `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 2_000_000
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `transport from a lower-level to a higher-level hospital in Vietnam` `, critical:` FALSE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`) `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
#ASSERT `the standard outcome of` (`a transport line by` `an ambulance of a hospital, of a lawful clinic, or of the 115 service` `, critical:` TRUE `, going with` NOTHING `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `not covered` `the benefit's own conditions are not met`
-- Transport is within benefit 1's limit: 49m already counted against it leaves 1m.
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `the standard illness event` `under` `the standard policy` `, counting` (`already` 49_000_000 `against` (`the limit for` `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`)) `, of` (`a transport line by` `an ambulance of a hospital, of a lawful clinic, or of the 115 service` `, critical:` TRUE `, going with` (JUST `Programme II benefit 1: hospitalisation for illness`) `, ordered by` NOTHING) EQUALS `payable` 1_000_000

§§ `Optional benefit 2 — outpatient treatment`
#ASSERT `the outcome, for the event` `an outpatient illness` `under` `the standard policy` `, of` (`an outside line under` `optional benefit 2: outpatient treatment` `for` `examination fee` `on` (YMD 2026 3 1) `of` 500_000 `at` `a hospital in Vietnam` `, ordered by` `the doctor's order`) EQUALS `payable` 500_000
-- 1.5m at one visit: the 1m limit per visit.
